  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment - Ice Profile Sonar",
  "description": "On 7-10 April 1976, the submarine USS Gurnard participated in the Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment (AIDJEX) by traversing 777 nautical miles along 3 tracklines in the Beaufort Sea. The resulting data set of ice thickness data originated from upward-looking acoustical soundings (sonar). Data are ice profiles, including latitude/longitude, ping interval, surface beam diameter, number of data points and ice thickness.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Create a data set to include ice thickness data originated from upward-looking acoustical soundings (sonar). Data are ice profiles, including latitude/longitude, upping interval, surface beam diameter, number of data points and ice thickness in the Beaufort Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23519402",
